                "explanation": "<strong>A</strong> <p>The acceleration vector\r                                 is found by taking the derivative of the velocity functions. (A),\r                                     <img src=\"images/85083c33aca3442798dd5442065a1878.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\">, is the only choice that correctly uses the Chain Rule on\r                                 both the <em>x</em> and <em>y</em> velocity functions.</p> <p>(B) and (D) have the\r                                 incorrect sign for the derivative of the sine function, and (C)\r                                 neglects the chain rule on the <em>y</em> velocity function.</p>"
